Z||000000||85 gt fiero||09-24-2001||03:15 PM||||I am painting my car 85 gt Rally Car and it is white now but i decided to paint it and was wonderen do you still have to prime it our just scuff it up with wetsand paper, also is it harder to paint fiberglass by yourself, one last thing what color looks best.        Thank You Randy ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sage||09-24-2001||09:22 PM||||If you're doing a color change you will want to prime everything first.  If you're repainting it the same color, and your paint is not in too bad a shape, you CAN get by withou it.  Keep in mind the surface you are putting the new paint on has to be super smooth.  In reality, you're top coat can only be as smooth as what's under it.<P>There's alot more to a "good" paint job than you might think, but you can get satisfactory results for a daily driver just messin around in your garage.<P>Good luck!||||reg||6
